A||N||4||gkozlov||Alternator Loose||||1||
Z||000000||gkozlov||12-20-2000||06:50 PM||||Ok here goes. My serpentine belt broke on my 86 SE 2.8. I bought and installed my new belt, but now I can't tighten my alternator. All it does is wobble. It wont slide back and forth for adjustment. I guess what I'm getting at is my belt is loose and I don't know how to tighten it.<P>Next question. I'm going to assume that the second belt is for my A/C. If so, is it safe to cut it off since my A/C is inop anyway? Will I benefit from doing this? How?<P>As always Thanks.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sign1_3.jpg">  <BR><A HREF="http://g.kozlov.tripod.com/gkozlov.htm" TARGET=_blank>GKozlovs Fiero Site</A>||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||12-20-2000||08:35 PM||||did you loosen both alternator bolts?<P>no, you don't need the AC belt on. However the compressor pulley will rust up. If you later decide to fix the AC you may have to replace the compressor. That assumes the compressor isn't why the system is dead now...<P>Will you gain anything with it off? probly not so you'd notice. It doesn't take much to just spin the pulley.<P>When my 4 cyl serpent let go today I replaced it with the non AC belt. My compressor clutch is broke and it's easier to get the non AC belt on from the top.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 12-20-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||gkozlov||12-20-2000||08:39 PM||||When I went o install my my new belt the alternator was already loosened, which would explaine the belt breaking and coming off. <P>The only bolt I could find is the one on the "slide" alternator bracket. Where is the other one?<P>This is why I'm not a mechanic.<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sign1_3.jpg">  <BR><A HREF="http://g.kozlov.tripod.com/gkozlov.htm" TARGET=_blank>GKozlovs Fiero Site</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||12-20-2000||08:54 PM||||Well post while I edit..... see if I care  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>there is a second bolt under it. That one is a long one. 6-8" long and passes thru the alternator.<P>The alternator and this bolt like to stick to each other. Once it's loose try to take it out and clean it up. then coat it with a thin film of grease before putting it back in.||||reg||1
Z||000004||gkozlov||12-20-2000||09:02 PM||||Thank you. I will try it tomorrow afternoon.<P>I want to take a minute to thank everyone thats helped my car stay on the road.<P>Thank you. There I said it.<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sign1_3.jpg">  <BR><A HREF="http://g.kozlov.tripod.com/gkozlov.htm" TARGET=_blank>GKozlovs Fiero Site</A>||||reg||1
